<InstitutionalPage
  title="Privacy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description="How Nuvellum handles reader analytics, Brief sign-ups and operational data."
  intro="Nuvellum collects less where less will do, and explains the services it actually uses."
  note="Google Analytics 4 loads only after a reader chooses “Allow”."
>
  <p>Nuvellum avoids unnecessary tracking. Where analytics are used, they are configured on a consent-first basis rather than loaded automatically for every visitor.</p>
  <h2>Reader analytics</h2>
  <p>Nuvellum uses Google Analytics 4 to understand page views, broad traffic sources and interactions such as article clicks, save actions, reading-depth milestones and successful Brief sign-ups. Nuvellum’s event layer does not send names, email addresses, search text, article-source URLs or URL query strings other than standard campaign tags such as utm_source. Google signals and advertising features are switched off.</p>
  <p>Google Analytics loads only after you choose “Allow” in the notice shown on your first visit. If you choose “No thanks”, no Analytics script or cookie is used. Your choice is remembered in this browser only. Analytics do not run on the unsubscribe page or the private editorial desk.</p>
  <p data-analytics-settings hidden><button type="button" class="aside-link quiet">Change analytics settings</button></p>
  <h2>Operational monitoring</h2>
  <p>Internal health checks observe publication output, repository checks and deployment state. They concern the condition of the publishing system, not the construction of reader profiles.</p>
  <h2>The Nuvellum Brief</h2>
  <p>If you subscribe to the Brief, Nuvellum stores your email address, the time of sign-up, the consent wording you accepted and the page from which you subscribed. That information is used only to deliver the Brief and is not sold or supplied for another party’s marketing. The list is kept in a private database (Upstash Redis, provided through Vercel), not in Nuvellum’s public repository or website files, and is visible only through the private editorial desk.</p>
  <p>To limit abusive sign-up attempts, Nuvellum may count recent attempts using a one-way, keyed fingerprint of your network address that expires within an hour; the address itself is not stored.</p>
  <p>Every Brief carries a personal unsubscribe link. Unsubscribing takes effect immediately. To request deletion of the underlying subscriber record, contact Nuvellum through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. The service used to deliver the Brief will be identified here when delivery begins.</p>
  <h2>Additional services</h2>
  <p>If advertising, accounts or other services materially change the collection of reader data, this page will be revised to state their purpose and the service responsible for processing that data.</p>
  <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
  <p>This policy is reviewed when the publication’s analytics, newsletter, advertising or account infrastructure changes materially.</p>
</InstitutionalPage>
